	skos:definition "An Index is an Observable which is computed based on the prices, rates or valuations of a number of assets that are tracked in a standardized way. Examples include equity market indices as well as indices on interest rates, inflation and credit instruments." , "The object to be observed is an Index, ie an observable computed on the prices, rates or valuations of a number of assets." ;
